  "notes": "B.S.E. Early Childhood Education (preschool through grade five licensure). Built from the official Kent State University program page 'Plan of Study Grid'. Minimum 2.750 overall GPA required for progression; admission to advanced study is required before upper-division education courses. Semester Four is a block (ECED 20101, 20102, 20103, 20105, 20192) taken together with a field assignment; Semester Five, Six, and Seven are also blocks that must be taken together in the same term with field assignments. Semester Eight is full-time teaching (ECED 40292 Internship in Elementary Schools, 9 cr). The catalog grid marks only critical-course placement, not per-course prerequisites; prereqs recorded here follow the course sequence (e.g., clinical sequence ECED 20192 -> ECED 30292 -> ECED 30392 -> ECED 40492; Teaching Early Readers ECED 30201 -> ECED 40402; MATH 14001 -> MATH 14002).",
